run.instructions:
Resolve this GitHub issue: '{{input.task.title}}' (#{{input.task.number}}) at {{input.task.externalUrl}}
{{input.task.description}}

Git is already authenticated for https (broker $GITHUB_TOKEN + credential helper), so clone/commit/push work, private repos included. Do: (1) derive the repo URL from the issue URL and `git clone <repo> repo && cd repo`; (2) checkout branch `tale/{{input.task._id}}` (create it if new, else `git fetch origin tale/{{input.task._id}} && git checkout` it); (3) if a pull request already exists for this branch, READ its open review comments (`gh pr view tale/{{input.task._id}} --comments` or the GitHub REST API) and address every blocking point — this is a re-work pass; (4) implement or refine the fix; (5) VERIFY IT YOURSELF — find the project's test/build command from its own config and run it until green; (6) `git add -A && git commit -m "Fix #{{input.task.number}}: {{input.task.title}}" && git push -u origin tale/{{input.task._id}}`; (7) if no pull request exists for this branch yet, open one to the repo's default branch (`gh pr create` or the GitHub REST API with $GITHUB_TOKEN) — otherwise your push already updated it. MANDATORY: write a summary of what you changed, the checks you ran, and the PR URL to /user/output/summary.md (absolute path).

